# Byte-integrity policy for content-pinned artifacts.
#
# Two repository artifact classes are verified by exact content:
#
#   * The packaged offline Go vulnerability snapshot carries a pinned SHA-256 in
#     src/before_deploy/controls/go_vulnerabilities.py.
#   * Every benchmark corpus manifest pins its source files by Git blob SHA-1.
#
# Both checks read working-tree bytes, so Git EOL conversion rewrites the very
# bytes they verify. With core.autocrlf=true (or a blanket `text=auto` rule) a
# Windows checkout converts these files to CRLF and the checks fail closed. That
# is not cosmetic: a converted working tree also produces a converted wheel, so
# the package would ship a snapshot that fails its own integrity check.
#
# Marking these trees as non-text disables EOL conversion and freezes the
# committed bytes on every platform. Do not add an EOL conversion rule for these
# paths, and re-run tests/unit/test_checkout_byte_integrity.py after changing
# anything here.
fixtures/** -text
src/before_deploy/controls/data/** -text
